    },
    {
      "id": "lj2vfn8",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "4. Troposphere"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "790399k",
      "content": "• Lowest layer of the atmosphere."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "iodev1g",
      "content": "• Contains about 75% of atmospheric mass."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "yel6qe4",
      "content": "• All weather phenomena such as clouds, rain and storms occur here."
    },
    {
      "id": "7ml4tr9",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "5. Stratosphere"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "h3db1s2",
      "content": "• Located above the troposphere."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "rb61mv0",
      "content": "• Contains the ozone layer that absorbs harmful ultraviolet radiation."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "0jk4c0o",
      "content": "• Jet aircraft often fly in this layer."
    },
    {
      "id": "adpikf0",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "6. Mesosphere"
    },
    {
      "type": "comparisonTable",
      "headers": [
        "Atmospheric Layer",
        "Key Characteristic",
        "Temperature Trend"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "Troposphere",
          "Contains almost all water vapor and weather phenomena",
          "Decreases with height (6.5°C per km)"
        ],
        [
          "Stratosphere",
          "Contains Ozone Layer; ideal for flying jet aircraft",
          "Increases with height"
        ],
        [
          "Mesosphere",
          "Meteors burn up here; coldest layer",
          "Decreases with height"
        ],
        [
          "Thermosphere",
          "Contains Ionosphere; reflects radio signals",
          "Increases rapidly with height"
        ],
        [
          "Exosphere",
          "Uppermost layer merging into outer space",
          "Extremely high kinetic temperature"
        ]
      ],
      "id": "q86eof9"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "fpt5af9",
      "content": "• Third layer of the atmosphere."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "lrqp5xo",
      "content": "• Meteors burn up due to friction in this layer."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "5lugepo",
      "content": "• It is the coldest layer."
    },
    {
      "id": "mar2u07",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "7. Thermosphere"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "nd5dyg4",
      "content": "• Temperature rises sharply with height."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "726cqtt",
      "content": "• Contains ionized gases forming the ionosphere."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "6a7ieea",
      "content": "• Important for radio communication."
    },
    {
      "id": "ojr65af",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "8. Exosphere"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "9e199kr",
      "content": "• Outermost layer of the atmosphere."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "e7btbvy",
      "content": "• Gradually merges into outer space."
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Questions frequently ask about the layer ideal for flying jet aircrafts (Stratosphere due to constant temperatures and lack of weather disturbances).",
        "The Ionosphere is located within the Thermosphere and facilitates radio transmission by reflecting radio waves back to Earth.",
        "The boundary where atmospheric temperature stops decreasing in the lowest layer is known as the Tropopause.",
        "Coldest atmospheric temperatures occur at the Mesopause, the upper boundary of the Mesosphere."
      ],
      "id": "izre5s9"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "i7fakzz",
      "content": "• Contains very thin air."
    },
    {
      "id": "wy3iypl",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Important Facts"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "at9lfl9",
      "content": "• Nitrogen is the most abundant gas in the atmosphere."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "vtffcxk",
      "content": "• Ozone layer is located in the stratosphere."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "3ui3dqq",
      "content": "• Troposphere contains most weather phenomena."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "gjjqf15",
      "content": "• Mesosphere is the coldest layer."
    }
  ],
  "enriched": true
}